java -Xms256m -Xmx2g <MainClassName>

Here is what those flags mean:
-Xms256m: Sets the initial (and minimum) heap memory size to 256 megabytes.
The JVM will start with this amount of memory allocated.

-Xmx2g: Sets the maximum heap memory size to 2 gigabytes.
The JVM will not be allowed to use more heap memory than this

, preventing it from consuming all your system's RAM.